# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
bin/
/aggrega
/aggrega-light
/aggrega-stripped
# scripts/build.sh --target names its outputs for the target system:
# aggrega[-light|-stripped]-<goos>-<goarch>, with .exe for windows.
/aggrega-*-*
/mutation-baseline

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out

# Output of aggrega cli
out/
dist/

# Exception: the pipeline test's golden tree stores pre-refactor build
# output as committed fixture data. The mirrored `dist/` subdirectory is
# intentional — it keeps the golden key shape identical to the renderer's
# emitted artifact map keys so the test compares like-for-like.
!internal/compiler/pipeline/testdata/golden-fullstack-app/dist/
!internal/compiler/pipeline/testdata/golden-fullstack-app/dist/**

# Embedded provider guests are reproducible build artifacts regenerated from
# guest source by scripts/build-embedded-*.sh (run via `go generate` on the
# embedded package or by scripts/build.sh). The .describe.json siblings are the
# describe() descriptors those same scripts extract from each guest, and the
# .plugin.yaml siblings are the complete Plugin entities generated beside them
# (machine describe() merged with the authored overlay). All three are
# regenerated by the build and not tracked; the .gitkeep placeholder stays
# tracked so the //go:embed all:plugins directory is always present.
internal/wasm/embedded/plugins/*.wasm.gz
internal/wasm/embedded/plugins/*.describe.json
internal/wasm/embedded/plugins/*.plugin.yaml

# The co-located plugin catalog is a developer-owned, regenerated-on-build
# convenience: each core guest's .wasm laid down beside its Plugin entity so the
# no-embed aggrega-light dev binary resolves core providers offline. It is
# opt-in (referenced only when a developer points catalog_dirs at it) and never
# part of a committed build, so it stays untracked like the embed artifacts it
# is derived from.
/.dev-catalog/

# Dependency directories (if you vendor)
vendor/

# Go workspace (developer-local)
go.work
go.work.sum

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local logs, env, editor swap files
*.log
.env
.env.*
*.swp
*.swo
